"Which statement best matches the excerpt’s combined description of DPO’s relationship to RLHF and its advantage over a naive preference-ratio objective?
(A) DPO abandons the RLHF-style KL-constrained reward objective in favor of directly maximizing the probability of preferred responses under a Bradley-Terry model; compared with a naive ratio objective, it avoids degeneration because preference learning happens after large-scale unsupervised pre-training.
