Answer:","You will be given an excerpt from 'Direct Preference Optimization: Your Language Model is Secretly a Reward Model'. Read it carefully and answer the multiple-choice question that follows.

Excerpt:
During the RL phase, the learned reward function is used to provide feedback to the language model. Following prior works~\citep{jaques2017sequence, jaques2020human}, the optimization is formulated as \begin{equation}\label{eq:RL} \max_{\pi_{\theta}} \mathbb{E}_{x\sim \mathcal{D}, y\sim \pi_{\theta}(y \mid x)}\bigl[r_{\phi}(x, y)\bigr] - \beta\mathbb{D}_{\textrm{KL}}\bigl[\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\mid \mid \pi_\text{ref}(y\mid x)\bigr], \end{equation} where $\beta$ is a parameter controlling the deviation from the base reference policy $\pi_\text{ref}$, namely the initial SFT model $\pi^\text{SFT}$. In practice, the language model policy $\pi_\theta$ is also initialized to $\pi^\text{SFT}$. The added constraint is important, as it prevents the model from deviating too far from the distribution on which the reward model is accurate, as well as maintaining the generation diversity and preventing mode-collapse to single high-reward answers.

