(A) It serves as a gauge-fixing condition inside each reward equivalence class: DPO chooses the unique representative whose reference-weighted exponentiated rewards sum to one for every prompt, which simultaneously makes the induced \(\pi(y\mid x)\) a normalized distribution and turns that same quantity into the optimal policy's partition function, yielding analytic tractability without reducing the set of representable rewards.
